# L §2.2: "the everyday words of the domain (age, discount, debt, share, order, rate, start, up) stay free
# for ids"; built-in names "are read as built-ins only directly before (", so any id ... may take one;
# rule labels may be keywords ("rule first", "rule none").  share = 2 rows, age = share + 1 (L §3.2 int + int).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

input share: int

def age: int at reader
  rule none = share + 1

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  share = 2

ask q1: age law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: 3
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
